Nikhil Kulkarni wrote:
>
> I am at level 14, with AC -6 and 122 HP. I am on the Samurai quest
> home level and I see a nurse there, so I expect the HP to go up a bit.
> I do have intrinsic telepathy and a uncursed luckstone. I have
> uncursed +0 GDSM, "oR and +0 Excalibur. Do you think I have a fair
> chance of successfully killing the priest in Minetown temple?
> I have never tried killing a priest before, so I am a bit hesitant to
> do that.

I have killed mine town priests with much weaker characters than that. 
Throw some items to find out your current missile range.  Dig out one of
the walls of the shrine so that distance is one past the altar (the
priest says at the altar +/- 1 square).  Gather a ton of missiles and a
few hundred rocks.  Drop them in batches small enough that you can pick
up plenty of new ammo without getting Burdened.  Start shooting.  If you
have planned your skill slots well you now have your bow skill up in the
multi-fire range so take with you have arrow you've ever found.  The
main danger in killing the prest with missile combat is being so slow
about it he starts generating flocks of insects.  Multifire handles
that.  Dance and multifire, multifire and multifire, dance and
multifire.  The faster and more deadly the barrage the better it works
but I have killed a few priests with only rocks more slowly.

> I am going to convert the DL 1 chaotic altar anyway.

It's closer but weaker monsters are spawned there.  If you want to do a
sacrifest the stronger the monsters the better because monster strength
counts towards reconcilation.  If all you want to do is BUC testing with
a small number of sacs mixed in just before you leave the level the
strength of the local monsters matters less.


